+# ION JOC Living Graph UI-domain workflow
+
+Status: **candidate workflow, not accepted canon**.
+
+This is the bounded workflow used for the Living Operational Graph cockpit slice. It is designed to prevent the prior failure mode where Codex built a simple monolithic vertical UI instead of a governed JOC work surface.
+
+## Agent route
+
+```text
+UI_CANON_STEWARD
+→ GRAPH_DATA_CARTOGRAPHER
+→ JOC_WORK_SURFACE_ARCHITECT
+→ COMPONENT_MASON
+→ A11Y_OPERABILITY_AUDITOR
+→ STATIC_VISUAL_PROOF_AUDITOR
+→ UI_SETTLEMENT_STEWARD
+```
+
+## Gates
+
+1. Load canon and current source package before coding.
+2. Preserve JOC shell zones:
+   - top rail
+   - left drawer
+   - central work surface
+   - right inspector
+   - bottom timeline
+3. Treat graph data as sample/candidate unless live adapters and receipts prove otherwise.
+4. Project all mounted graph nodes/edges before adding decorative 3D/R3F effects.
+5. Expose data honesty, proof gates, routes, selected-object truth, and timeline evidence.
+6. Run model tests, static proof harness, and build validation.
+7. Require browser screenshot proof and operator review before any UI acceptance claim.
+
+## Non-claims
+
+This workflow does not settle UI state, approve production deployment, or claim live telemetry.
